436	  // Port forwarding is what makes the `ssh root@host -p <port>` line below true
437	  // for a NAT server. If it cannot be proved, the readiness message says so
438	  // instead of printing a command that will hang (H5 + M7 #10). Not fatal: the
439	  // VM itself is fine and a failed PROVISION would flip it to ERROR and release
